From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karl Godard <karl@minimal.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 21:53:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/vsock: stop polling a unix proxy closed by a full
 shutdown

When the guest shuts down both directions of a stream mapped to a host
unix socket, UnixProxy::shutdown() shuts down the host socket, marks the
proxy Closed and returns the release update, but leaves the fd registered
for EventSet::IN until the reaper removes the proxy.

On Linux the shut-down socket reports EPOLLHUP, process_event() takes the
HANG_UP arm, and that arm disarms the fd. The macOS epoll emulation maps
an EOF on EVFILT_READ to IN | READ_HANG_UP, never HANG_UP, and
process_event() ignores IN on a proxy that is not Connected. The
level-triggered read filter therefore stays ready, and the muxer thread
wakes on it in a tight loop until the reaper drops the proxy.

Disarm the fd in the full-shutdown branch, as the other paths that close
a proxy already do.

Upstream: https://github.com/libkrun/libkrun/pull/916
Signed-off-by: Karl Godard <karl@minimal.dev>
Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/unix.rs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/unix.rs b/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/unix.rs
index d50269f..90550de 100644
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/unix.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/unix.rs
@@ -614,6 +614,7 @@ impl Proxy for UnixProxy {
         self.push_reset();
         let mut update = self.release();
         self.status = ProxyStatus::Closed;
+        update.polling = Some((self.id, self.fd.as_raw_fd(), EventSet::empty()));
         update.signal_queue = true;
         update
     }
